WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.730
Speaker 1: There is a stunning new poll from
YouGov which finds that 66 percent of Americans,

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:12.730
I'm sorry, of Republicans in the southern
United States want to secede from the United

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:14.230
States and become their own country.

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:19.810
This was a joint poll between YouGov and Bright
Line Watch, and they did some interesting

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:21.010
things.

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:25.180
One of the things that the poll does is it
breaks down the country by regions.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:30.220
So you've got like the Pacific region, which
is California, Washington, Oregon, Hawaii

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:31.550
and Alaska.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:34.150
You've got all these, the Northeast, etc.

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:39.770
And what they did was they reported people's
interest in separating out as a country, not

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:41.630
at the state level, but as a region.

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:48.090
If your region could become its own country,
would you want to secede from the United States?

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:51.740
And they asked people this on the basis of
party affiliation.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:57.770
So let's look at some examples here in the
northeast region as an example, which includes

00:00:57.770 --> 00:01:02.920
Maine, New Hampshire, Vermont, New York, Pennsylvania,
Massachusetts, Connecticut, Rhode Island,

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:05.219
you know, a couple of Maryland, Delaware.

00:01:05.219 --> 00:01:09.680
They said, OK, would you want to be your own
country and secede from the United States?

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:13.840
And for example, thirty nine percent of Democrats
said, yes, we do.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.870
We would like to be our own region.

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:19.590
Thirty five percent of independents and only
twenty six percent of Republicans said I would

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:22.530
like the Northeast to be our own region.

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:28.030
The largest level of support in this poll
across all regions and political IDs is southern

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:29.799
Republicans.

00:01:29.799 --> 00:01:34.710
If you look at the southern region that includes
Texas, Florida and a bunch of other states,

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:38.950
66 percent of Republicans said, yeah, I want
to secede.

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:43.369
I would like our region, the southern region,
to be its own country.

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:49.340
Now, the absolute most ironic thing about
this is that the southern region would be

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:52.799
completely unsustainable economically.

00:01:52.799 --> 00:01:53.799
Some of.

00:01:53.799 --> 00:01:59.819
The states that are the biggest takers rather
than givers when it comes to federal money

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:04.459
would be in that southern region, so set a
different way.

00:02:04.459 --> 00:02:10.899
Some of the states that are the most dependent
on money that comes from other states through

00:02:10.899 --> 00:02:19.349
the federal government are Mississippi, Kentucky,
South Carolina, Louisiana, Alabama, Tennessee,

00:02:19.349 --> 00:02:20.939
Arkansas and Oklahoma.

00:02:20.939 --> 00:02:25.269
They're all in what would be this southern
region of the United States.

00:02:25.269 --> 00:02:27.239
Texas and Florida are kind of in the middle.

00:02:27.239 --> 00:02:28.239
They're not terrible.

00:02:28.239 --> 00:02:30.760
They're not great in terms of paying in versus
getting out.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:36.810
So the point here is the group that most wants
to secede from the United States, Southern

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:42.459
Republicans, and make their own country out
of their region are the ones whose states

00:02:42.459 --> 00:02:47.549
are the least economically able to do that
and the most dependent on blue states to subsidize

00:02:47.549 --> 00:02:48.549
them.

00:02:48.549 --> 00:02:49.549
This isn't new.

00:02:49.549 --> 00:02:50.549
We've covered this.

00:02:50.549 --> 00:02:53.310
We've done stories about this before, about
this contrast before.

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.019
It's been true for a very long time.

00:02:55.019 --> 00:02:58.150
Now consider the reality versus perception.

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:03.049
Their perception is things are really bad
being part of the United States.

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:04.049
Why?

00:03:04.049 --> 00:03:11.250
Because of Democrats and liberals and progressives
like Joe Biden's communism and his socialism

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:15.400
and the Marxist Democrats WOAK culture is
ruining us.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:20.730
Cancel so-called culture is ruining us men
in girls sports as they love to say.

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:22.620
It's ruining the country.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:24.930
And we'd be better off if we separated and
did our own thing.

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:27.450
That's the perception that many of them have.

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:29.939
The reality is none of that stuff is actually
going on.

00:03:29.939 --> 00:03:35.390
There are almost no socialists in the Democratic
Party and however bad things are in your state

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:38.549
in terms of education and they're very bad
in a lot of these states.

00:03:38.549 --> 00:03:42.920
However, bad things are in your state in terms
of access to health care infrastructure, it

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:47.989
would be even worse if you lost the subsidies
you get from blue states through the federal

00:03:47.989 --> 00:03:53.390
government, blue states that are paying in
much more than they get out and making your

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:58.269
education system be slightly less terrible,
making your health care system be slightly

00:03:58.269 --> 00:04:03.140
less terrible, making your infrastructure
slightly less terrible, it couldn't possibly

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:04.140
be more backwards.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:08.299
And they have the idea these Southern Republicans,
if we separated and did our own thing, we

00:04:08.299 --> 00:04:09.599
would be much better off.

00:04:09.599 --> 00:04:15.890
But again, in a sense, just like I don't take
joy in the anti vaccine nurse that just died

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:19.620
of covid because I see her as a victim of
disinformation.

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:25.319
It's very similar for lots of these people
who wrongly blame their problems on imaginary

00:04:25.319 --> 00:04:30.819
issues rather than the real failures of their
almost exclusively Republican state and local

00:04:30.819 --> 00:04:32.310
level elected officials.

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:35.360
They are also the victims of disinformation.

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:39.120
They are persistently victims, by the way,
also.

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:44.660
Of a terrible education system in their states,
they can't even follow simple logic like,

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:51.020
oh, pandemic, OK, mask for now and then vaccine
once we can get it, they can't even follow

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:52.020
that.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:53.850
So they are also victims to some degree.

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:57.120
Now, we'll have a voice mail about this with
a different perspective a little bit later

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:58.120
